{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cd4wfk4tPzEzjsuavWga7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WjP1vQRVie3SBYvyZ93bgg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\PC-220627-03\\.claude\\projects\\C--Users-PC-220627-03-Desktop-project-task-ticket-kata-w1\\memory\\stale-target-cross-branch-tests.md","content":"---\nname: stale-target-cross-branch-tests\ndescription: Run `mvn clean test` in this kata — plain `mvn test` leaks other branches' feature files from a stale target/\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nThis kata keeps each new requirement on its own branch (`gateway-swap`, `ticket-limit`, …), and each\nbranch carries its own `src/test/resources/features/*.feature`. `target/` is not branch-aware, so\n`mvn test` after switching branches runs the *previous* branch's compiled feature files out of\n`target/test-classes` alongside the current branch's, producing `UndefinedStepException` failures for\nsteps that legitimately do not exist on this branch.\n\n**Why:** on 2026-07-16 the gateway-swap work looked broken because a stale `ticket_limit.feature`\nfrom the `ticket-limit` branch failed — the actual change was fine and all real scenarios passed.\n\n**How to apply:** always verify with `mvn clean test` here. If a feature file appears in the test run\nbut `find`/git shows it only under `target/`, it is cross-branch pollution — do not implement its\nsteps (that would also mean editing the off-limits `src/test/` files).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":48498,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":828},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"50c88bf5-24f5-41ab-85e7-023b996a3b75","uuid":"